{
  "title": "Forest & Flowers",
  "introduction": [
    "In Forest & Flowers, sculpted leaves, blossoms, and bark rise from layers of acrylic and organic plaster. As the light shifts, rivers, hidden figures, and metallic traces come into view. These paintings explore love, remembrance, and our dependence on the natural world."
  ],
  "artworks": [
    {
      "id": "mother-nature",
      "slug": "mother-nature",
      "title": "Mother Nature",
      "dimensions": "24 × 36 in.",
      "medium": "Mixed-media acrylic with organic plaster on canvas",
      "description": [
        "A hidden goddess emerges from the forest, her profile formed by the leaves, vines, and flowers that surround her. Beside her, a pale river winds between densely textured mountains, drawing the eye into the landscape. Sculpted foliage and metallic highlights reveal a presence that might initially go unnoticed.",
        "Mother Nature considers the contradictions in our relationship with the natural world: we depend on its generosity, yet often mistake that dependence for ownership. She sustains us, inspires us, and reclaims what we leave behind. Her beauty rewards curiosity; her strength exists beyond our permission. The painting asks us to look more closely, and to recognize the difference between appreciating nature and believing we control it."
      ],
      "copyStatus": "artist-source",
      "availability": "provisional",
      "availabilityNote": "Availability to be confirmed",
