    {
      "id": "gilded-bloom",
      "slug": "gilded-bloom",
      "title": "Gilded Bloom",
      "dimensions": "24 × 36 in.",
      "medium": "Mixed-media acrylic with organic plaster on canvas",
      "description": [
        "A partial bloom extends inward from the edge of the canvas, its golden and copper-toned petals set against layered washes of green, blush pink, and cream. Fine grooves mark the petals, while a rougher central surface creates a contrast in texture. Subtle blue and purple undertones beneath the warmer colors reveal themselves as the light and viewing angle change.",
        "Developed through experimentation with color, layering, and organic form, Gilded Bloom gives curiosity a visible presence. Broad passages of paint leave room around the flower, allowing its contours and metallic nuances to emerge gradually. The composition rewards close attention to the small variations through which the painting took shape."
      ],
      "copyStatus": "artist-source",
