    {
      "id": "a-forest-forgotten",
      "slug": "a-forest-forgotten",
      "title": "A Forest Forgotten",
      "dimensions": "24 × 36 in.",
      "medium": "Mixed-media acrylic with organic plaster on canvas",
      "description": [
        "A towering tree trunk fills the center of A Forest Forgotten, its deeply worked surface rising beyond the canvas. Around it, sculpted leaves and pale flowers frame glimpses of green forest beneath a sky of pink, gold, and blue. The close viewpoint gives the tree a commanding presence while allowing the surrounding landscape to remain partly concealed.",
        "Inspired by the conservation work of Paul Rosolie and Junglekeepers, the painting reflects on the beauty and vulnerability of rainforests, and on the distance between recognizing their value and acting to protect them. It brings that concern into a tangible encounter with bark, foliage, color, and scale.",
        "10% of the sale price of this original artwork will be donated to Junglekeepers in support of its Amazon rainforest conservation efforts."
      ],
      "copyStatus": "artist-source",
      "availability": "provisional",
