    {
      "id": "moss-and-mushrooms",
      "slug": "moss-and-mushrooms",
      "title": "Moss & Mushrooms",
      "dimensions": "30 × 40 in.",
      "medium": "Mixed-media acrylic with organic plaster on canvas",
      "description": [
        "Deep diagonal grooves carry the eye across the bark of an old forest tree. Earthy browns and fine golden highlights trace its ridges, interrupted by vivid patches of green moss. Clusters of sculpted mushrooms project from the surface, their rust-colored tops and pale edges creating small, distinct pauses within the sweeping grain.",
        "From a distance, Moss & Mushrooms reads as an abstract arrangement of lines, color, and movement. Closer viewing reveals the individual forms inhabiting the bark. This shift in perspective is central to the painting: a surface easily passed by becomes a landscape of its own, full of detail and quiet life."
      ],
      "copyStatus": "artist-source",
      "availability": "provisional",
      "availabilityNote": "Availability to be confirmed",
