      "dimensions": "24 × 36 in.",
      "medium": "Mixed-media acrylic with organic plaster on canvas",
      "description": [
        "75 Leaves pays tribute to WWII pilot Wallace N. “Wally” King. Each of its 75 sculpted leaves represents one of the 75 combat missions he flew. A blue-and-gold current, representing the Elbe River, winds through layered passages of green, pink, and metallic texture.",
        "Among the foliage, a single golden-bronze leaf stands apart: a tribute to King’s life and a reminder that humanity and hope can endure amid war. The flowing composition brings these meanings into an organic landscape, holding courage and sacrifice alongside the beauty of life. Its details invite a slower reading, allowing the tribute to emerge through the individual leaves and the river moving among them."
